# Trivy vulnerability ignore list.
# Applies to both the pr-gate.yml `trivy fs` scan and the nightly.yml
# container image scans (Trivy reads .trivyignore from the working directory).

# CVE-2026-27456 — util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when setting up loop devices.
# No fixed util-linux version is available yet in the mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0
# base image (Trivy reports no "Fixed Version"). Exploitation requires a local
# unprivileged user plus an /etc/fstab entry using `user,loop` options pointing at an
# attacker-writable path. Our containers run a single non-root app process (USER app)
# with no multi-user shell access and no such fstab entries, so the attack precondition
# does not exist in how these images are deployed.
# Revisit and remove once the base image ships a patched util-linux (>= 2.41.4).
CVE-2026-27456

# The following OS-package CVEs have no fixed version available yet upstream (Trivy
# reports a blank "Fixed Version") in the mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0 base image.
# Each requires an API surface or execution context this container never exercises:
# single-process ASP.NET Core app running as non-root `USER app`, no local multi-user
# shell, no PKCS#11 RPC server, no journald ForwardToWall, no direct calls to the
# specific deprecated glibc resolver/iconv functions involved.
#   - CVE-2026-6238, CVE-2026-5435, CVE-2026-4438, CVE-2026-4437, CVE-2026-4046 (libc6/libc-bin):
#     deprecated glibc resolver-print functions (ns_printrr/fp_nquery), gethostbyaddr with a
#     DNS nsswitch backend, and iconv() with the IBM1390/1399 charsets — none of which this
#     app calls.
#   - CVE-2026-13757 (libp11-kit0): unbounded recursion in the PKCS#11 RPC message parser;
#     no PKCS#11 RPC server runs in this container.
#   - CVE-2025-5222 (libicu74): stack overflow in the `genrb` resource-bundle compiler tool,
#     which is not invoked at runtime by this app.
#   - CVE-2024-2236 (libgcrypt20): timing side-channel in libgcrypt's RSA path; .NET's crypto
#     stack does not route through libgcrypt.
#   - CVE-2024-56433 (login/passwd — shadow-utils): default /etc/subuid range; irrelevant with
#     no local multi-user accounts.
#   - CVE-2026-40228 (libsystemd0/libudev1): systemd-journald ANSI-escape forwarding, gated on
#     `ForwardToWall=yes` and a local multi-user terminal; neither exists here.
#   - CVE-2026-27171 (zlib1g): unbounded loop in crc32_combine64/crc32_combine_gen64, reachable
#     only via a caller-supplied crc32 combine call this app never makes.
# Revisit and remove entries individually once each package ships a fix upstream.
CVE-2026-6238
CVE-2026-5435
CVE-2026-4438
CVE-2026-4437
CVE-2026-4046
CVE-2026-13757
CVE-2025-5222
CVE-2024-2236
CVE-2024-56433
CVE-2026-40228
CVE-2026-27171
